latest_plan = "Based on the reflection, here's a detailed step-by-step plan to solve the challenge:\n\n1. Analyze the input grid:\n   a. Determine grid dimensions.\n   b. Identify the background color (most frequent color).\n   c. Create a list of all non-background colors.\n\n2. For each non-background color, calculate a comprehensive score:\n   a. Frequency score:\n      - Count the number of cells with this color.\n      - Calculate the ratio of this count to total non-background cells.\n\n   b. Structural importance score:\n      - Identify connected components of this color.\n      - Calculate the average size of these components.\n      - Assign higher scores to colors forming larger connected areas.\n\n   c. Pattern formation score:\n      - Check for line formations (horizontal, vertical, diagonal).\n      - Identify symmetrical patterns.\n      - Detect shapes like crosses, squares, or clusters.\n\n   d. Color interaction score:\n      - Count the number of unique colors adjacent to this color.\n      - Calculate the ratio of cells of this color that are adjacent to other colors.\n\n   e. Distribution score:\n      - Divide the grid into sectors (e.g., 3x3 sectors).\n      - Calculate the number of sectors where this color appears.\n      - Assign higher scores to colors with wider distribution.\n\n   f. Positional importance score:\n      - Assign higher scores to colors appearing in central positions.\n      - Give additional points for presence at intersections of other color regions.\n\n   g. Multi-scale presence score:\n      - Analyze the grid at different scales (2x2, 4x4 blocks).\n      - Calculate the color's significance at each scale.\n\n3. Combine the scores:\n   - Normalize each score component to a range of 0-1.\n   - Assign weights to each score component (e.g., structural importance might have a higher weight than frequency).\n   - Calculate a weighted sum of all score components for each color.\n\n4. Select the most significant color:\n   - Choose the color with the highest combined score.\n   - In case of a tie, prioritize based on structural importance and color interaction scores.\n\n5. Generate the output:\n   - Create a new 1x1 ColoredGrid with the selected color.\n\n6. Implement error handling and edge cases:\n   - Handle cases where all cells are the same color.\n   - Ensure the algorithm works for grids of different sizes.\n\n7. Optimize and refine:\n   - Test the solution against all provided examples and the failing test case.\n   - Fine-tune the weights and scoring methods based on the results.\n   - Ensure the algorithm is efficient for larger grids (up to 30x30).\n\n8. Validate the solution:\n   - Run the algorithm against all test cases.\n   - Verify that it produces the correct output for each case.\n   - If any discrepancies are found, analyze them and adjust the algorithm accordingly.\n\nThis plan aims to create a comprehensive scoring system that considers multiple aspects of color significance. By breaking down the problem into these steps, we can systematically evaluate each color's importance and select the most significant one based on a holistic assessment."
